  "text": "ordinarium.praefatio-apostolorum",
  "about": "The Preface of the Apostles. It asks the eternal Shepherd not to forsake His flock, but to preserve it under the protection of the Apostles and their successors.",
  "segments": {
    "s01": { "narrative": "Then the priest separates his hands and holds them apart until the end of the Preface. When it is finished, he joins them again and, bowing, says: Sanctus." },
    "s02": { "translation": "It is truly meet and just, right and profitable for salvation:" },
    "s03": { "translation": "To entreat Thee humbly, O Lord, that Thou, eternal Shepherd, wouldst not forsake Thy flock, but through Thy blessed Apostles wouldst keep it under constant protection:" },
    "s04": { "translation": "That it may be governed by those same rulers whom Thou didst appoint over it as pastors and vicars of Thy work." },
    "s05": { "translation": "And therefore with Angels and Archangels, with Thrones and Dominions, and with all the hosts of the heavenly army, we sing the hymn of Thy glory, evermore saying:" }
  },
